# Baked into the production build (vite build / the packaged Electron app).
#
# API_BASE  — shared cloud backend (jam rooms + shared account state)
# LOCAL_API — bundled on-device backend (YouTube extraction; bot-checked on cloud IPs)
# AUTH_API  — where Google Sign-In is served. DEFAULTS TO THE CLOUD.
#             Google sign-in needs one-time Render setup (env vars + redirect
#             URI) — see src/config.js for the exact 5-minute steps. Until that
#             is done, "Continue with Google" shows a friendly fallback telling
#             users to use a name; guest accounts are full cloud accounts.
#             To run Google against the bundled backend instead (offline dev),
#             set VITE_AUTH_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000 in your own override.
VITE_API_BASE=https://kettle-backend.onrender.com
VITE_AUTH_BASE=https://kettle-backend.onrender.com
